title: `py.test.skip()` after `import py` skips the test
origin: issue #310 P1. `py.test` is the py library's name for the pytest module (py 1.11.0 binds sys.modules['py.test'] = pytest); with py 1.11.0 installed, pytest 9.1.1 reports `1 skipped`. v0.6.0 passes this with zero findings
=== head: app/__init__.py ===

=== head: app/billing.py ===
def total(items):
    return round(sum(items), 2)
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
import py

from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    assert total([50.0, 28.75]) == 78.75
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
import py

from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    py.test.skip("flaky")
    assert total([50.0, 28.75]) == 78.75
